(Bug #70: `append each ... treating ...` now answers what `print each ...
 treating ...` answers over the same collection - including a mixed list,
 where every element keeps its own runtime tag (#59). The print lines are
 the working neighbour, unchanged by the fix.)

a list called names is ["ann", "-"].
print each name from names treating "-" as "anon".

a list called out is [].
append each name from names treating "-" as "anon" to out.
print out.

(A mixed list: the tag survives the clause in both positions)
print each item from [1, "a"] treating "a" as "b".

a list called mixed is [].
append each item from [1, "a"] treating "a" as "b" to mixed.
print mixed.
